# .trivyignore — governed vulnerability exceptions for the scan:image gate.
#
# Each line is either a comment (`#`) or a vulnerability ID (CVE-XXXX-XXXXX).
# The scan:image job runs `trivy image --ignorefile .trivyignore --exit-code 1`,
# so any ID listed here is excluded from the blocking gate.
#
# GOVERNANCE POLICY — non-negotiable:
#   1. Every ignored CVE MUST have a ticket reference in a trailing comment.
#   2. Every ignored CVE MUST state the reason (upstream pending, false positive,
#      accepted risk with compensating control, etc.).
#   3. Entries are reviewed QUARTERLY. A scheduled job warns on entries older
#      than 90 days (planned: scheduled:trivyignore-review).
#   4. `--ignore-unfixed` is already set globally — only CVEs WITH a published
#      fix need to be listed here. Unfixable CVEs are filtered automatically.
#
# FORMAT:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # <TICKET> <component> <reason> <review-date YYYY-MM-DD>
#
# EXAMPLE (uncomment and adapt when the first pipeline run surfaces findings):
# CVE-2024-XXXXX  # LKV-1234 keycloak upstream patch pending, review 2026-09-30
